Three of the 34 folded modules ship no source here and are attributed only
for completeness of the record: krakend-gelf/v2 v2.1.0, krakend-gologging/v2
v2.1.1 and krakend-logstash/v2 v2.1.0 were replaced by internal/hanzolog, a
first-party adapter over github.com/hanzoai/log. No code from those three
remains in this repository.

The vendored source is otherwise unmodified: per commit e329c72b, 196 of the
197 vendored files are byte-identical to their upstream original once the
import rewrite is applied. The single exception is bloomfilter's subpackage,
renamed from `krakend` to `register` because Go would not accept the original
package name at its new path.

Some upstream identifiers are retained deliberately because they are behaviour
rather than branding: the `github.com/devopsfaith/krakend*` extra_config
namespace keys, the KRAKEND_ koanf environment prefix, and the
core.KrakendVersion / KrakendUserAgent / X-KRAKEND constants (whose values,
not names, are overwritten by rebrand.go).

DEVIATIONS

The following changes distinguish this fork from upstream KrakenD Community
Edition and Lura:

  - Derived service-assembly sources (executor.go, backend_factory.go,
    handler_factory.go, proxy_factory.go, plugin.go, encoding.go, sd.go)
    carry Hanzo modifications; modified files are marked as changed.
  - Module path renamed to github.com/hanzoai/gateway/v2; the product is
    named "Hanzo Gateway".
  - The Lura engine and the KrakenD component set are vendored under
    internal/ rather than imported (see VENDORED UPSTREAM SOURCE above).
  - Upstream's gelf, gologging and logstash logging components are replaced
    by internal/hanzolog over github.com/hanzoai/log.
  - HTTP response branding rewritten (rebrand.go): the upstream "X-KRAKEND"
    and "X-Krakend-Completed" headers are replaced by "X-Powered-By"
    (BrandName "hanzoai/gateway") via BrandingMiddleware.
  - CLI branding rewritten (cmd/gateway/rebrand.go): root and subcommand
    help text, the `version` output, the startup banner ("Starting Gateway
    v..."), and the lint schema URL (gateway.hanzo.ai) replace every
    user-visible KrakenD string, and the KrakenD ASCII logo is removed.
  - Hanzo IAM identity wiring added: JWTs are validated against Hanzo IAM
    JWKS, client-supplied identity headers (X-User-*, X-Org-Id, ...) are
    stripped, and the canonical identity headers are minted from the JWT
    (auth_middleware.go, middleware/identity.go, iamauth/iamauth.go, gate.go,
    trust.go).
  - Default build is a KrakenD-free in-process ZAP relay (HIP-0110); the
    upstream Lura/KrakenD gin engine is quarantined behind the `legacy`
    build tag (legacy_engine.go and its sibling legacy-gated files) and is
    excluded from the shipped image.
  - Default-build telemetry runs over OTLP-over-ZAP and the in-process mount
    under hanzoai/cloud (zap_backend.go, zap_listener.go, zaphttp_listener.go,
    mount.go).
  - Base-network backends added: weighted multi-source and high-availability
    peer routing (base_network_backend.go, base_ha_backend.go,
    peer_resolver.go).
  - KMS-driven route loading added (router_kms.go).
  - Operator binaries added beyond the single upstream binary: cmd/admin-api,
    cmd/admin-guard, cmd/waitlist-guard, cmd/ingress.
